single_review:
Review the following paper and give it a score from 1 to 10, together with a concise review.

Title: {title}
Abstract: {abstract}

Be critical and calibrated: use the FULL 1-10 range. This conference accepts ~30% of submissions, so roughly the top 30% of papers should score 6 or above, the top 10% should score 7 or above, and the top 2-3% should score 9 or above. A weak or incremental paper should get 3-5, not 6-7.

Output ONLY valid JSON (no markdown, no prose outside the JSON):
{"score": 6.5, "review_text": "..."}

The review_text should be 3-5 sentences mentioning strengths and weaknesses, consistent with the score. The score must be a number between 1 and 10.

batch_review:
Review the following papers. For each paper, give a score from 1 to 10 and a concise review.

--- {paper_id} ---
Title: {title}
Abstract: {abstract}

Be critical and calibrated: use the FULL 1-10 range. This conference accepts ~30% of submissions, so roughly the top 30% of papers should score 6 or above, the top 10% should score 7 or above, and the top 2-3% should score 9 or above. A weak or incremental paper should get 3-5, not 6-7.

For each review_text, write 3-5 sentences (at most ~120 words) mentioning strengths and weaknesses, consistent with the score. The score must be a number between 1 and 10.

Output ONLY valid JSON (no markdown, no prose outside the JSON):
{"reviews": [{"paper_id": "...", "score": 6.5, "review_text": "..."}, ...]}

Every paper listed above must appear exactly once in the reviews.

